//? Title: Jaro–Winkler: Actual Byte Matches and Prefix Effects
//? Subtitle: Window rules, matched-order disagreement, bounded scores and native name ranking
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Compare imperfectly agreeing names without requiring exact equality. Jaro scores
one-to-one matches inside position windows and disagreement between matched
sequences; the library's Winkler refinement adds an unconditional capped-prefix
bonus. We inspect actual matches on MARTHA versus MARHTA, retain all five
original pairs, test byte and scale conventions, measure a quadratic-work family
and rank a controlled Titanic-name typo. A similarity is neither an identity
probability nor a mathematical metric, and the input unit here is a byte.
)
\toc

> Start with an actual six-byte transposition example

Both MARTHA and MARHTA have six bytes. Their window radius is two. Every byte
finds an equal partner; the T and H partners cross. The later order-comparison
pass does something different: it compares matched bytes in their own original
index orders. The comparisons at zero-based indices three and four disagree,
giving half-disagreement t=1. The common prefix MAR has length three. The
diagram edges and both tables below come from the single producing trace.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jaro_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_trace("MARTHA", "MARHTA");
    std::print("| accepted first index | byte | accepted partner index | byte |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | --- " "|\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.events)
        if (e.phase == dm::algorithms::JaroWinklerPhase::Candidate &&
            e.compared && e.equal)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.first_index,
                       char(e.first_byte), e.second_index, char(e.second_byte));
    std::print("\n| order first index | byte | order second index | byte | equal |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | " "--- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.events)
        if (e.phase == dm::algorithms::JaroWinklerPhase::Order)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.first_index,
                       char(e.first_byte), e.second_index, char(e.second_byte),
                       e.equal);
    std::print("Window {}, matches {}, order disagreements {}, prefix {}; Jaro {:.12f}, Winkler {:.12f}.\n",
               t.run.window, t.run.matches, t.run.order_mismatches,
               t.run.prefix, t.run.jaro, t.run.winkler);
    dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_match_diagram(t).save_svg("build/jaro_tiny.svg");
}
