> Controls: windows, bytes, scales and the metric claim

AB and BA have the same multiset of bytes but window zero, so their base score
is zero. Case is significant: MARTHA and martha have no equal byte. Embedded NUL
is an ordinary byte, not a terminator. The UTF-8 encodings C3A9 and C3AA
represent different code points but share their leading byte, giving this
byte-based implementation a positive score. No Unicode decoding, normalization,
case folding, accent removal or tokenization is performed.

An especially clear metric counterexample uses A, AA and BA. If distance is one
minus Jaro, d(A,BA)=1 but d(A,AA)+d(AA,BA)=1/6+1/3=1/2. The triangle inequality
fails. The prefix-refined distance fails on the same triple. A bounded
similarity therefore does not justify metric indexing or an identity probability
interpretation.

The two scale curves also expose the unconditional policy. Four shared bytes
followed by ten unrelated suffix bytes produce J below0.7, yet still receive a
prefix bonus. The short different-suffix pair and this low-base pair both reach
one at p=0.25. That is the stated convex-combination rule, not evidence of
identity.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jaro_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const std::vector<std::tuple<std::string, std::string, std::string>> cases{
        {"same bytes outside windows", "AB", "BA"},
        {"case difference", "MARTHA", "martha"},
        {"two distinct UTF-8 code points", "\xC3\xA9", "\xC3\xAA"},
        {"embedded NUL", std::string("A\0B", 3), std::string("A\0C", 3)},
        {"empty convention", "", ""},
        {"odd disagreement count", "ABCDEF", "BCADEF"}
    };
    std::print("| control | window | matches | order disagreements | prefix | Jaro | Winkler |\n| --- | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto & [label, a, b] : cases) {
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_run(a, b);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} |\n", label,
                   r.window, r.matches, r.order_mismatches, r.prefix, r.jaro,
                   r.winkler);
    }
    const double direct = 1 - dm::algorithms::jaro_similarity("A", "BA");
    const double through =
        (1 - dm::algorithms::jaro_similarity("A", "AA")) + (
        1 - dm::algorithms::jaro_similarity("AA", "BA"));
    std::print("Metric counterexample: direct distance {:.12f}, sum via AA {:.12f}.\n",
               direct, through);
    std::vector<double> scales, short_score, low_score;
    std::print("\n| scale | short different suffix | long unrelated suffix |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int i = 0; i <= 5; ++i) {
        const double scale = .05 * i;
        scales.push_back(scale);
        short_score.push_back(dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_similarity("ABCDx",
                                                                      "ABCDy",
                                                                      scale));
        low_score.push_back(dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_similarity(
                            "ABCDxxxxxxxxxx", "ABCDyyyyyyyyyy", scale));
        std::print("| {:.2f} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} |\n", scale,
                   short_score.back(), low_score.back());
    }
    bool invalid = false, bytes = false, events = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_similarity("", "",
                                                       std::numeric_limits<
                                                       double>::quiet_NaN());
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        invalid = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_trace("A", "A", .1, {1, 0});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        bytes = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_trace("A", "A", .1, {2, 2});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        events = true;
    }
    std::print("Invalid scale rejected: {}. Complete-byte cap rejected: {}. Two-event cap rejected before " "the third inspection: {}.\n",
               invalid, bytes, events);
    if (!invalid || !bytes || !events)
        throw std::runtime_error("control mismatch");
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(scales, short_score, "short suffix", {35, 95, 210}, 2).points(
        scales, short_score, "short suffix", {35, 95, 210}, 4).line(
        scales, low_score, "long suffix", {210, 55, 40}, 2).points(
        scales, low_score, "long suffix", {210, 55, 40}, 4).legend(
        {"short suffix", "long suffix"}, {{35, 95, 210}, {210, 55, 40}}).title(
        "Unconditional prefix scales: bounded does not mean identical").x_label(
        "prefix scale p").y_label("actual refined similarity").ylim(.4, 1.2).save_svg("build/jaro_controls.svg");
}
