> Count work and derive a quadratic control

An occupied candidate slot is visited but performs no byte equality test. Once
matching ends, the order pass performs one byte comparison per matched first
index. The prefix pass performs at most four comparisons, including the first
mismatch when present. These are selected logical operations, not timings or
physical memory/cache access counts.

For strings consisting of n copies of A and n copies of B, no slot is occupied
and every candidate fails. For an equal even length, w=n/2−1. Summing the
clipped window lengths gives

$$
C_n=n(2w+1)-w(w+1)=\frac{3n^2-2n}{4}.
$$
\alttext(The all-nonmatching equal-even-length family visits exactly three quarters n squared minus one half n candidate slots.)

There are no order comparisons and exactly one failed prefix comparison. This is
a deterministic quadratic worst-case work control, not a runtime benchmark.
General work is O(n+m+n*min(m,2w+1)) and flag workspace O(n+m). Recording adds
O(E+n+m) owned data for E actual events and copied input bytes; an event limit
is useful because the history can be quadratic too.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jaro_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::vector<double> nvalues, actual, formula;
    std::print("| bytes per string | actual candidate slots | exact window sum | actual byte tests | order " "tests | prefix tests |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n = 8; n <= 512; n *= 2) {
        const auto r =
            dm::algorithms::jaro_winkler_run(std::string(n, 'A'),
                                             std::string(n, 'B'));
        const auto expected = (3 * n * n - 2 * n) / 4;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n,
                   r.work.candidate_slots, expected,
                   r.work.candidate_byte_tests, r.work.order_byte_tests,
                   r.work.prefix_byte_tests);
        if (r.work.candidate_slots != expected)
            throw std::runtime_error("window-count identity");
        nvalues.push_back(double(n));
        actual.push_back(double(r.work.candidate_slots));
        formula.push_back(double(expected));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(nvalues, formula, "exact window sum", {95, 95, 95}, 2).points(
        nvalues, actual, "actual slots", {35, 95, 210}, 5).legend(
        {"exact model", "actual slots"}, {{95, 95, 95}, {35, 95, 210}}).title(
        "A deterministic quadratic candidate-inspection family").x_label(
        "bytes per input string n").y_label("selected candidate-slot visits").ylim(-5000, 240000).save_svg("build/jaro_work.svg");
}
```
