> Ownership, limits, reference and scope

Scalar legacy functions retain their signatures and valid-scale operation order.
Complete score comparisons against the frozen implementation are bitwise equal
for the verified control corpus. Finite scales in[0,0.25] are now enforced for
all Winkler calls, including empty inputs. The pure Jaro function omits prefix
comparisons. Overflow-safe window endpoints replace the old unchecked index sum.
No function changes caller strings or retains caller references.

Run/trace options default to one million combined input bytes and one million
actual event records. Complete byte admission precedes flags and trace input
copies. An event is admitted before the candidate, order or prefix inspection;
no partial history returns if a limit or allocation fails. Zero disables an
optional cap; size/container/counter checks remain. Untraced calls ignore the
event ceiling, and legacy scalar functions disable optional caps. The byte cap
counts each borrowed input once even though a trace owns a copy; it is not a
total allocation quota. Working flags, scalar summaries, capacities and
byte/peak RAM are excluded. Empty-input score conventions bypass flag work.

Rank defaults admit up to10000 candidates and one million total query/name
bytes. k=0 still validates complete input but performs no scoring. Duplicate
names remain different rows, and returned names/scores are owned. Ranking adds
O(N log N) comparisons and O(N plus longest-pair length) working storage to all
pair-scoring costs, plus owned top-k name copies. There is no score replay or
shared mutable state. The diagram has a separate complete byte display quota and
validates displayed accepted edges; it does not certify the provenance of an
edited history.

[Winkler's original1990 paper|https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/ED325505.pdf]
discusses prefix-adjusted string comparators and distinguishes comparator values
from a complete record-linkage decision procedure. Its string-comparator and
weighting context was inspected directly. This report states the library's
specific longer-length window, greedy byte rule and linear unconditional prefix
formula, rather than claiming agreement with every historical or thresholded
variant. The [Jaro1989 reference|https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1989.10478785]
is Advances in Record-Linkage Methodology as Applied to Matching the1985 Census
of Tampa, Florida, JASA84(406),414–420.

The original pair scores are preserved, the work model matches every measured
point, and the constructed Titanic typo ranks its source first. The byte, prefix
and triangle controls explain why none of those outcomes establishes
Unicode-aware matching, a metric distance or calibrated entity identity.

> Verification

Twenty-two selected native cases pass CTest and AddressSanitizer plus
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. This includes43923 exhaustive byte-string/scale
traces over NUL, A and FF, exact accepted partners and ordered comparisons, odd
disagreement counts, UTF-8/NUL/empty controls, scale saturation/rejection,
input/event/ranking caps, ownership, graphics and the existing string-metric
suite. Frozen-code comparisons preserve712480 scalar score results bitwise
